1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:08,599
A mango!

3
00:00:08,869 --> 00:00:11,139
Inside it, there is one big seed.

4
00:00:11,419 --> 00:00:12,689
We plant the seed.

5
00:00:12,999 --> 00:00:14,589
What will it grow into first?

6
00:00:14,649 --> 00:00:15,929
One, a mango.

7
00:00:17,159 --> 00:00:18,339
Two, a flower.

8
00:00:19,589 --> 00:00:21,109
Three, a young plant.

9
00:00:22,593 --> 00:00:24,103
Hold on to your answer!

10
00:00:25,975 --> 00:00:28,425
A little snail is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:28,705 --> 00:00:29,905
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:30,035 --> 00:00:32,015
Snails love cool, damp places.

13
00:00:32,085 --> 00:00:35,305
It hides somewhere new each time, so look under the leaves!

14
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,820
You against the Buddies!

15
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:38,940
Lock in first with your fingers.

16
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:41,040
One finger for every point.

17
00:00:41,621 --> 00:00:42,921
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:44,956
Observing like a scientist.

19
00:00:45,159 --> 00:00:46,739
What grows from a seed.

20
00:00:46,945 --> 00:00:48,335
Measuring a plant.

21
00:00:48,836 --> 00:00:49,776
Are you ready?

22
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:50,986
Three!

23
00:00:51,366 --> 00:00:52,026
Two!

24
00:00:52,396 --> 00:00:53,046
One!

25
00:00:53,466 --> 00:00:54,186
Go!

26
00:00:55,575 --> 00:00:56,465
Round one!

27
00:00:56,775 --> 00:00:58,995
What will the mango seed grow into first?

28
00:00:59,275 --> 00:01:00,585
Show me your fingers!

29
00:01:04,058 --> 00:01:05,038
Locked in!

30
00:01:05,166 --> 00:01:05,886
One!

31
00:01:06,016 --> 00:01:08,816
A mango seed grows into a mango, of course!

32
00:01:08,866 --> 00:01:13,446
Two. I think a pretty flower comes out first, and then the mango.

33
00:01:13,493 --> 00:01:14,233
Three!

34
00:01:14,323 --> 00:01:17,263
Every big tree starts small, so I think it grows into a

35
00:01:17,283 --> 00:01:18,733
young plant first!

36
00:01:19,013 --> 00:01:20,993
But a seed grows so slowly.

37
00:01:21,013 --> 00:01:23,209
How will we ever know what comes first?

38
00:01:23,229 --> 00:01:26,059
We plant it, and we watch it like a scientist.

39
00:01:27,915 --> 00:01:28,775
I know!

40
00:01:28,885 --> 00:01:31,425
I will look at it once now, and once more when it

41
00:01:31,445 --> 00:01:32,627
is a big tree.

42
00:01:32,647 --> 00:01:35,841
But then we will miss all the changes in between, Momo!

43
00:01:35,861 --> 00:01:37,011
Look closer.

44
00:01:37,581 --> 00:01:41,911
A scientist observes again and again, and writes down what the senses

45
00:01:41,931 --> 00:01:42,580
tell us.

46
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,600
I look at it.

47
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:45,489
Our seed is brown, big and flat.

48
00:01:45,509 --> 00:01:47,099
I touch it gently.

49
00:01:47,299 --> 00:01:49,424
It feels hard, and a little bit hairy.

50
00:01:49,444 --> 00:01:50,654
And I smell it.

51
00:01:50,724 --> 00:01:52,459
It still smells of mango!

52
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:55,859
We use our senses, and we write it down every time.

53
00:01:56,429 --> 00:01:58,379
This is called observing.

54
00:01:59,499 --> 00:02:03,869
Observing means looking, touching and smelling carefully, again and again, like a

55
00:02:03,889 --> 00:02:05,169
plant detective!

56
00:02:07,871 --> 00:02:09,031
Say it with me!

57
00:02:09,738 --> 00:02:13,168
We can use our five senses to gather information about the life

58
00:02:13,188 --> 00:02:14,598
cycles of plants.

59
00:02:17,826 --> 00:02:18,976
Look closer.

60
00:02:19,566 --> 00:02:21,966
Here is our seed, under the soil.

61
00:02:22,546 --> 00:02:25,266
We made a window in the pot, so we can see it.

62
00:02:25,783 --> 00:02:26,623
Day ten!

63
00:02:26,763 --> 00:02:30,453
A tiny root pokes out first, and it grows down, down, down.

64
00:02:30,659 --> 00:02:31,909
Day twenty.

65
00:02:32,119 --> 00:02:35,589
Now a shoot pushes up, bent like a hook, towards the light.

66
00:02:35,795 --> 00:02:36,965
Day thirty.

67
00:02:36,995 --> 00:02:38,335
Two leaves open!

68
00:02:38,455 --> 00:02:39,845
But they are red, not green.

69
00:02:39,865 --> 00:02:41,429
Is it sick?

70
00:02:41,449 --> 00:02:42,769
It is not sick.

71
00:02:43,349 --> 00:02:45,559
New mango leaves are red at first.

72
00:02:46,129 --> 00:02:47,719
Watch them turn green.

73
00:02:48,233 --> 00:02:49,003
And look!

74
00:02:49,103 --> 00:02:51,853
The old seed is still there, at the bottom of the stem,

75
00:02:51,873 --> 00:02:54,143
like a lunch box for the young plant!

76
00:02:56,772 --> 00:02:59,052
The answer is three: a young plant!

77
00:02:59,342 --> 00:03:00,412
Three fingers?

78
00:03:00,682 --> 00:03:01,892
One finger up!

79
00:03:01,945 --> 00:03:05,105
A plant with a thin stem and a few leaves is called

80
00:03:05,125 --> 00:03:06,165
a young plant.

81
00:03:07,325 --> 00:03:09,335
A young plant is like a baby tree.

82
00:03:09,485 --> 00:03:11,655
It has no flowers and no fruits yet!

83
00:03:11,776 --> 00:03:13,116
Be the mango seed!

84
00:03:13,396 --> 00:03:14,376
Shrink down.

85
00:03:14,656 --> 00:03:15,586
Quietly.

86
00:03:17,876 --> 00:03:20,306
You are a mango seed, under the soil.

87
00:03:21,146 --> 00:03:23,216
It is dark, cool and quiet.

88
00:03:23,741 --> 00:03:24,971
Days go by.

89
00:03:25,751 --> 00:03:28,971
You swell, and a tiny root pushes out of you, and grows

90
00:03:28,991 --> 00:03:29,651
down.

91
00:03:30,175 --> 00:03:33,285
Then a shoot pushes up, up, up, through the soil, into the

92
00:03:33,305 --> 00:03:34,015
light!

93
00:03:34,537 --> 00:03:37,257
Your first leaves open, soft and red.

94
00:03:38,057 --> 00:03:39,617
You are a young plant now!

95
00:03:41,424 --> 00:03:42,714
Say it with me!

96
00:03:43,429 --> 00:03:45,459
The seed grew into a young plant.

97
00:03:48,083 --> 00:03:50,493
Our young plant grows taller every week.

98
00:03:50,693 --> 00:03:52,613
Let's measure it with a ruler!

99
00:03:52,739 --> 00:03:55,979
We can use simple tools, such as a ruler, to help us

100
00:03:55,999 --> 00:03:57,579
measure the height of plants.

101
00:03:58,316 --> 00:03:59,216
My turn!

102
00:03:59,306 --> 00:04:01,616
I put the ruler on the table, under the pot.

103
00:04:01,696 --> 00:04:03,886
Our plant is twenty centimetres tall!

104
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:05,570
Something is not right.

105
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:08,020
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

106
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,260
Hold on!

107
00:04:14,673 --> 00:04:15,803
Arms crossed?

108
00:04:16,073 --> 00:04:17,283
One finger up!

109
00:04:17,335 --> 00:04:19,485
The pot is not part of the plant.

110
00:04:19,625 --> 00:04:22,435
Put the zero of the ruler on the soil, where the stem

111
00:04:22,455 --> 00:04:23,405
comes out.

112
00:04:23,528 --> 00:04:24,188
Oops!

113
00:04:24,328 --> 00:04:27,268
So our young plant is really twelve centimetres tall.

114
00:04:27,508 --> 00:04:28,878
Still very handsome!

115
00:04:29,007 --> 00:04:30,467
Show me your score hand!

116
00:04:30,747 --> 00:04:32,137
One finger or more?

117
00:04:32,457 --> 00:04:33,817
You beat the Buddies.

118
00:04:34,087 --> 00:04:35,117
Two fingers?

119
00:04:35,397 --> 00:04:36,407
High five!

120
00:04:36,979 --> 00:04:38,409
Did you spot the snail?

121
00:04:38,699 --> 00:04:40,649
It was on the rim of our plant pot!

122
00:04:40,779 --> 00:04:42,359
Here is a fun fact!

123
00:04:42,549 --> 00:04:45,599
A snail has thousands of tiny teeth on its tongue.

124
00:04:45,809 --> 00:04:49,149
It scrapes up soft young leaves, so gardeners keep an eye on

125
00:04:49,169 --> 00:04:50,339
their young plants!

126
00:04:50,467 --> 00:04:51,747
Tell someone at home!

127
00:04:52,476 --> 00:04:54,676
Let's read today's key words together!

128
00:04:54,966 --> 00:04:55,726
Ready?

129
00:04:56,013 --> 00:04:56,913
Observing.

130
00:04:58,357 --> 00:04:59,157
Seed.

131
00:05:00,432 --> 00:05:01,482
Young plant.

132
00:05:02,936 --> 00:05:03,876
Well done!

133
00:05:04,673 --> 00:05:07,683
Our young plant has no flowers and no mangoes yet.

134
00:05:07,723 --> 00:05:09,513
Will it ever grow mangoes?

135
00:05:09,533 --> 00:05:10,933
Good question, Momo!

136
00:05:11,213 --> 00:05:14,123
The big old mango tree downstairs will show us.

137
00:05:14,187 --> 00:05:15,777
Find out in Part Two!

138
00:05:16,937 --> 00:05:18,038
Say it with us!

139
00:05:18,838 --> 00:05:19,588
Ready?

140
00:05:19,711 --> 00:05:20,371
One!

141
00:05:20,711 --> 00:05:21,411
two!

142
00:05:21,716 --> 00:05:22,891
Now you know!
